Experiment                    : This experiment compares run time and resource consumption of Benchbase queries in different DBMS.
Benchbase data is generated and loaded using several threads. Loading uses a batch size of 128 rows per INSERT.
Benchmark is 'tpcc'. Scaling factor is 16. Target is based on multiples of '1024'. Factors for benchmarking are [1, 16]. Benchmarking runs for 5 minutes.
Experiment uses bexhoma version 0.11.5.
System metrics are monitored by a cluster-wide installation.
Experiment is limited to DBMS ['PostgreSQL'].
Import is handled by 1 processes (pods).
SUT is fixed to cl-worker36.
Storage is swept across configurations: nvme, cephcsi, size 50Gi. Persistent storage is removed before every repetition.
Loading is tested with [1] threads, split into [1] pods.
Benchmarking is tested with [16, 64] threads, split into [1] pods.
Benchmarking is run as [1] times the number of benchmarking pods.
Experiment is run 3 times.
Maximum DBMS across the whole cluster is 1.
Results are validated against basic correctness requirements.
